    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, we r having a big issue at the plant. we're running sublimation prints on polyester blends but the color transfer is super inconsistent. some areas look bright but most of the design is coming out faded or washed out. we're checking the heat press temps and they seem steady at 200c. what else should i be looking at to fix this?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Check for improper fabric prep like lint or starch residue that can interfere with adhesion, and ensure the sublimation film score side is fully touching the substrate. It might also be that your heat press is not applying consistent pressure across the entire design, even if the temperature reads correctly. Finally, verify you are using genuine sublimation inks compatible with your specific polyester blend ratio, as standard ink can fail on lower polyester content fabrics.",
      "source": "target",
