    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "we checked the pressure and the ink is definitely the right stuff. we even swapped out the heat press to see if it was a machine issue but the same thing happens. it's like the ink is there on the paper but it just won't stay or it's like the color just vanishes during the press. it's really frustrating because it's so random where it fails. any idea why the ink would just... not take?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The randomness suggests the heat isn't actually reaching critical levels in specific areas, potentially caused by uneven plate contact or thermal settling rather than a blown fuse. On polyester blends, the heat must penetrate deep into the fiber; if the polyester blend has a low fiber percentage, it may simply not absorb enough energy to turn the ink into gas. I recommend lowering your cycle time slightly while increasing the pressure to improve dwell time at the interface, and ensuring your release settings allow for enough total heat application time.",
      "source": "target",
